ESP-IDF (Espressif IoT Development Framework) is the official development
framework for the ESP32 family of SoCs.

It provides a CMake-based build system, a component library for common
peripherals, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth stacks, OTA updates, partition
management and FreeRTOS integration.

The framework is driven by idf.py, a Python tool that builds, flashes and
monitors ESP32 projects.  Cross-compiling firmware additionally needs the
xtensa-esp32-elf (or riscv32-esp-elf) toolchain, which is not part of
this port.
